                <pb facs="0392" n="293" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg293"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.5151/814: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-02-06T18:00:00-03:00">February 6, 1936—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 6—5:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. American interests here have received telegraph advices that Export-Import
                    Bank has formulated certain objections to frozen credits agreement and has
                    threatened to withdraw its commitments.</p>
                <p>Should appreciate any information Department can give me for my guidance.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
